    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d217">

                <pb facs="0543" n="501" sameAs="frus:frus1951v04p1/pg501"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 217</seg>
                </opener>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">840B.062/4–1851: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iceland (Lawson) to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reykjavik</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-04-18T18:00:00+00:00">April 18, 1951—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>210. Inform Mitchell Defense.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d217-f1"/> Fon Min has just
                    informed me of govt’s great concern possibility Commie directed strike set for
                    May 18 which he says cld easily take on character of general strike. Said govt
                    as well as social dems taken by surprise but will do everything possible prevent
                    serious widespread strikes.</p>
                <p>He very fearful US troops will arrive here near that date which he thinks wld be
                    embarrassing us as well as Ice Govt, especially if there port difficulties re
                    off-loading our equipment, supplies etc. He suggests date not later than May 3.
                    Can we meet that date having troops, as well as survey party alerted to meet
                    that date when confirmed? I recommend we make every effort.</p>
                <p>Fon Min confident agreement will be signed in plenty of time to permit such
                    programing.</p>
                <p>Pls comment soonest.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lawson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d217-f1" n="1" xml:id="d217-f1-content">
                <p>The message was relayed to the Department of Defense on April 19 at 1 a.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
